What is OSI Layer : 
      The OSI (Open Systems Interconnection) Model is a 7-layer conceptual framework used to understand how data travels from one device to another over a network.
      It standardizes networking communication into layers.

Why OSI Model is Important?
      Helps troubleshoot network issues
      Explains how data flows
      Used in networking interviews
      Foundation for TCP/IP understanding

Layer Number	                     Layer Name	                  Function
7	                                 Application	         User interaction (HTTP, FTP)
6	                                 Presentation	         Encryption & Formatting
5	                                   Session	           Session management
4	                                  Transport	           End-to-end delivery (TCP/UDP)
3	                                   Network	           Routing (IP address)
2	                                    Data               Link	MAC address, Frames
1	                                  Physical	           Cables, Signals

Real-Life Example (Opening Google)

Let’s say you type: www.google.com
Layer 7 – Application  - Browser sends HTTP request.
Layer 6 – Presentation - Data gets encrypted using SSL/TLS (HTTPS).
Layer 5 – Session - Session established between client and server.
Layer 4 – Transport - TCP establishes 3-way handshake.
Layer 3 – Network - IP address added for routing.
Layer 2 – Data Link - MAC address added.
Layer 1 – Physical - Bits travel through cable/WiFi.
